nodes.statement:
There are unique series $A,B\in x+x^2\Q[[x]]$ satisfying, respectively,
\begin{align}
 A(x^2+2x^3+2A(x)^2)&=3A(x)^2,\\
 B(3x^2)&=2x^2+B(x)^2-2B(x)^3.
\end{align}
Both series have integer coefficients. Moreover,
\begin{align}
 A(x)^{3k}&\equiv A(x^3)^k\pmod3 &&(k\geq0),\\
 A(x)^2&\equiv x^2+2x^3\pmod9,\\
 B(x)^3&\equiv B(x^3)\pmod3,\\
 B(x)^2&\equiv x^2+2B(x^3)\pmod3.
\end{align}
